    -- What's New (UI/WhatsNew.lua)
    "Your Alts' Queues Work Together", "Hover an item to see how many your crafting queues need, how many you still have to buy, and which of your characters' queues are making it. Queue bolts on your tailor and your engineer's shopping list drops them and lists the cloth instead. Ore says what it smelts into, and Queue Needed queues exactly what's missing in one click.",
    "Queue Your Enchants", "Queue an enchant with a quantity to plan and shop for its materials. Each one you apply with the Enchant button comes off the queue.",
    "\"On Shopping List\" on item tooltips, how many a craft makes on the recipe icon, a smarter auction verdict when disenchanting, crafted reagents priced at their crafting cost, options in categories with a live tooltip preview, and a pile of fixes. The changelog has every detail.",
    "Set Up Camp", "A new Camp window (footer, quick button or /pf camp) lists every camp feature you hold, can craft, have on an alt or haven't learned yet. Place them with one click, and the shared cooldowns sit right at the top.",
    "Bind one key: it puts on your fishing gear, best pole and lure, casts, and catches when the fish bites. Your normal gear goes back on when you mount or stop fishing, and bites are louder so you don't miss the splash.",
    "Send Stuff by Hand", "The Transfer Planner's letter button opens Manual Transfers: send an alt an item or some gold, or ask one to send you something. Drop a stack from your bags straight on the window. At the mailbox, Mail attaches exactly the right amount, splitting stacks for you. You can ask for gear from Disenchanting Mode too.",
    "Keys for Your Quick Buttons", "Bind a key to any window, to Disenchanting Mode or to each of your professions. Hover a button and press a key to bind it (/pf bind). New Overview and Settings buttons, plus rows or columns, growing from any corner.",
    "Your Queue on Item Tooltips", "Hover an item and see how many your crafting queues need and how many you still have to buy. Hold Shift for who needs it and for which recipes.",
    "Smarter Reagent Prices", "A crafted reagent costs whichever is cheaper, buying it or making it. A Bolt of Silk Cloth is priced at four Silk Cloth when that's less, and Cost to Craft shows what it's made from.",
    "Options, Sorted", "The options are now in categories, and a new Tooltips section lets you switch every line on or off and drag the blocks into any order, with a live preview beside it.",
    "And More", "A two-row footer when it fills up, a Disenchanting footer cell, a note when a newer version is out, and a pile of fixes. The changelog has every detail.",
    "Quick buttons", "A little bar that opens your cooldowns, Transfer Planner, shopping list, queue and Disenchanting Mode without the main window, each with a count of what's waiting. It can have a button for each of your professions too. Drag it wherever you like.",
    "Hit the dust icon on the Enchanting tab and your recipes turn into a list of everything you could disenchant. See what each piece might give, whether it's worth more vendored, disenchanted or on the auction house, and zap it right there. Your alts' gear shows up too.",
    "Disenchant advice on tooltips",
    "Hover a weapon or armour piece and it'll tell you whether to disenchant, vendor or auction it. Every disenchant you do gets recorded, so over time you'll see how the real drops stack up against the odds.",
    "Check in on your alts",
    "Pick any of your characters on the Overview to browse their recipes, and queue crafts for them. Whoever's holding the materials gets told what to mail over.",
    "A shopping list that keeps itself",
    "Whatever your queues are short of lands on the list on its own, shared across all your characters on the same faction. Your old lists came along for the ride.",
    "Mail counts now",
    "Stuff sitting in a mailbox counts as yours. At the mailbox, the Transfer Planner mails your alts what they need and grabs what your queue needs in one click.",
    "A smarter crafting queue",
    "Queue something and the bits it needs get queued first. Short on materials? It won't burn them all on the first step and leave the final craft hanging.",
    "Tidier windows",
    "The queue, Transfer Planner and shopping list share one row of buttons, the side windows all match in width, and docked windows never fall off the screen. With the main window closed, they cozy up to the mailbox or bank instead.",
    "And a whole lot more",
    "Recipe Search, the Skill Up Route (with SkillUp Forever), trainer and vendor locations without needing Questie, an Integrations page, and a pile of fixes. The changelog has every last detail.",
    "Got It",
